\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Sequence likelihood ratio}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{policy-optimization}
\tag{importance-sampling}

\p{Let #{\pi_b} be the behavior policy that generated
#{y=(y_1,\ldots,y_n)} and let #{\pi_\theta} be the current policy. The
per-token likelihood ratio and the \strong{sequence likelihood ratio} are}

##{
  \rho_t(\theta)
  =\frac{\pi_\theta(y_t\mid x,y_{<t})}
         {\pi_b(y_t\mid x,y_{<t})},
  \qquad
  \rho_{\mathrm{seq}}(\theta)
  =\prod_{t=1}^{n}\rho_t(\theta).
}

\p{The ratios are defined only where the behavior probabilities in their
denominators are positive. The factorization follows from the autoregressive
law.}

\p{Policy likelihood ratios enter the PPO surrogate in
\citet{Section 3}{schulman2017proximal}. RLVR objectives may clip token ratios
rather than the complete sequence ratio, so the two quantities must remain
distinct.}
